# Shell scripts must keep Unix line endings whatever the machine they are
# edited on. This repo is worked on from Windows, and a .sh checked out with
# CRLF fails on Linux with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" — which looks nothing
# like a line-ending problem and would take the API down on the next deploy,
# since server/start.sh is the start command.
*.sh text eol=lf
